    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2BWDp9cgemxzr2hZ9jvXJcG)_\n\nFollow-up to #471.\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Base: `main`; #471 is already merged. Touches only `sp-citations` (`.el`, its section in `sp-academic.org`, the preload test).\n- Branch is `claude/project-thread-d7whd6`, not number-prefixed: a cloud session cannot rename a branch after the PR number is known.\n\n## Causes\n\n- **`(setf citar-cache--bibliography-buffers)` is void:** `sp-citations.el` loads before `citar` does. When Emacs loads a file it expands `setf` and `cl-pushnew` at once; the accessor was unknown, so the expansion became a call to a function named `(setf citar-cache--bibliography-buffers)`, which does not exist. Reproduced in batch with the same message; this hit every file.\n- **No `citar-bibliography.eld`:** the file was written only at the end of a pass that finished. The pass died on the first file, and nothing wrote it at exit either.\n\n## Changes\n\n- The slots `entries`, `props` and `buffers` are read with `cl-struct-slot-value` and set with `aset` at `cl-struct-slot-offset`, never with `setf` on the accessors (`sp-citations-preload--slot`, `--set-slot`).\n- `sp-citations-preload--compatible-p` checks the variable, the three functions and the three slots before the first file. If they differ, the preload says so once in the echo area and stays off.\n- The disk cache is written when the pass ends, when it stops on an error or `C-g`, and on `kill-emacs-hook`. Each time only if citar's entry tables differ from the last write, or the file does not exist, so a parse done by a `citar` call is saved at exit too.\n- Docs updated as bullets; no CHANGELOG edit; no `when-let`.\n\n## Tested\n\n- `tests/sp-citations-preload-test.el`: 11 tests pass on Emacs 29.3 against a stand-in for `citar-cache`.\n- The test file now loads the preload code with `load` before the struct exists, as Emacs does. With the old `setf` style the tests fail with `void-function \\(setf\\ citar-cache--bibliography-buffers\\)` (checked); with the fix they pass.\n- New tests: cache file written; saved after an error and at exit; not rewritten when nothing changed; preload off when citar's functions are missing.\n- `tools/check-tangle.sh`: the `.el` is what the doc tangles to.\n\n## Not tested\n\n- Still nothing ran against the real `citar`, `parsebib` or your bibliography; the container has no citar, and I could not reach your Elpaca sources, so the internals come from citar's `main` branch on GitHub. If your installed citar differs, the preload should now say so instead of failing on every file.\n- No timings.\n- Whether `aset` on the cache object works with your citar's struct definition: tested only on a stand-in `cl-defstruct`.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [ ] `cd ~/dotfiles; git fetch origin claude/project-thread-d7whd6; git checkout claude/project-thread-d7whd6`, restart Emacs\n- [x] `emacs -Q --batch -l tests/sp-citations-preload-test.el -f ert-run-tests-batch-and-exit` passes\n- [x] After about 5 s idle: `*Messages*` shows `Updating bibliography ...` for each `.bib`, no `citar preload:` error\n- [x] If it says `citar preload is off: ...`: send me that message (your citar has other internals)\n- [x] `M-x citar-open` right after: no `Updating bibliography` and no wait\n- [x] The file `citar-bibliography.eld` exists in `sp-cache-dir` once the pass is done\n- [ ] Quit and restart: the pass shows no `Updating` lines for unchanged files\n- [ ] Edit and save one `.bib`: only that file is read again after the idle delay\n- [ ] `C-g` during a parse: preload stops, `citar-open` still works\n\n<details><summary>Revert after testing</summary>\n\n- `git -C ~/dotfiles restore .`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles switch main && git -C ~/dotfiles pull`; restart Emacs.\n- Delete `citar-bibliography.eld` in your cache dir for a cold start.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiCyfpEM7dFcJmFXN4v)_",
